 "captions": [
  {
   "from_frame": 0,
   "duration_frames": 240,
   "text": "We ran two hundred and sixty-six recordings through a machine. Twenty-seven came back with the wrong product name in them."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 240,
   "duration_frames": 288,
   "text": "You type up a call, forward the summary, and somebody acts on it. The page reads finished, so nobody rereads it. Nothing is underlined."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 528,
   "duration_frames": 348,
   "text": "It does not fail at random. It fails on the parts that carry no context: proper nouns, figures, and anything said only once. The sentences around them stay clean."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 876,
   "duration_frames": 372,
   "text": "So the check is small. Five fields, the same five every time. Names, numbers, dates, decisions, and who owes what. Here it is running against one of the bad files. There."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 1248,
   "duration_frames": 480,
   "text": "And here is what it does not catch on its own. When the machine writes a name as another real word every single time, the page still reads clean. So check the five against the recording, not against the page."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 1728,
   "duration_frames": 228,
   "text": "The five fields are in the caption, not behind a comment. Send this to whoever types up your calls."
  }
 ],
